    "narrative": "With our roster facing a collection of mid-tier arms today, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor, boasting an elite 74.74 score. Despite facing a tough arm in Cole, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a significant dynamic platoon advantage that keeps his ceiling high for power and counting stats. Close behind, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) capitalize on favorable matchups against Bradish and Holmes, respectively. **Sam Antonacci** remains a critical engine in our pursuit of stolen bases, and his position at the top of the order maximizes his efficiency despite the neutral park environment. **Heliot Ramos** also projects as a strong start at 65.99; while his score is tempered slightly by the need to contend with Bradish\u2019s hold potential, his middle-of-the-order slotting ensures he remains a primary driver for RBI production.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day was **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just short of the starting rotation with a 36.77 score. While **Nasim Nunez** represents our most volatile threat on the basepaths, the optimizer penalized his projected ninth-hole assignment and the daunting task of facing deGrom. The combination of deGrom\u2019s elite skill profile and the lack of high-leverage opportunities at the bottom of the order made it impossible to justify starting him over more stable options like **Drake Baldwin**, who holds a solid 64.69 projection while batting second. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Wade Meckler**, whose 48.71 score is heavily contingent on his lead-off status; should the official lineup shuffle him down, his marginal value will drop further. **Miguel Vargas** rounds out the starters at 59.39, offering a steady floor against Holmes. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** all inactive due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is heavily taxed, leaving no room for high-upside gambles. We will rely on our core of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Sam Antonacci** to carry the load today, keeping a close eye on the weather and any late-breaking lineup changes for **Wade Meckler** and **Nasim Nunez**.",
